WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:13.440
But let's have a look down.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.443
What we are going to cut

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.512
You see the plum tree?

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.515
It’s blossoming right now

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.155
This one, I think, is fine.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.757
Let's cut this one away.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:45.091
Yeah.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.995
And then very carefully cut this one... Do you have a hand saw?

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.164
Yeah. I have a hand saw

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.766
And you can use the cutter over there

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.738
Yea it’s easier... I’ll do it with the chainsaw

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:02.075
oh no no... i’ll be very careful

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.012
Yeah, but this is round.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.915
So you'll damage it anyway.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.918
with the chainsaw I’m more precise than with this

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:15.221
Really? Yea

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.656
It’s your tree, haha

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.291
Yeah. Oh.

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:29.796
It’s beautiful, how quick it goes

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.501
Flowers?

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:20.533
She smells nice!

00:13:13.492 --> 00:13:13.959
Yeah.

00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:16.962
In fact, you cut a slice

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:21.367
You eat it,
and it's not enough 

00:13:22.201 --> 00:13:24.503
So you cut another one, and another one

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:27.506
and another one.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.275
Yeah.

00:13:29.275 --> 00:13:30.976
Did you grew up in Como?

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:31.811
Yeah.

00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:32.444
Oh, really?

00:13:32.444 --> 00:13:34.413
I think the most beautiful places in the world

00:13:34.413 --> 00:13:37.116
Does it feel like that to you? Or is it just a normal place?

00:13:37.116 --> 00:13:40.019
What do you think is one of the most
beautiful places in the world?

00:13:40.019 --> 00:13:40.953
Lake Como? Yea

00:13:40.953 --> 00:13:42.655
I don't think so.

00:13:42.655 --> 00:13:44.857
Nobody thinks so in Italy

00:13:44.857 --> 00:13:48.027
It's pretty nice! It's beautiful!

00:13:48.027 --> 00:13:51.130
Well I can understand it is gentrified, touristic, etc...

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:55.668
No, I really enjoy the lake in summer especially

00:13:56.302 --> 00:13:59.305
and I appreciate where I live, but

00:13:59.905 --> 00:14:03.375
but as a local you also see some problems

00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:09.882
More in the administration of the city

00:14:16.789 --> 00:14:20.125
Also the dog is looking

00:14:20.125 --> 00:14:22.127
very interested

00:14:22.127 --> 00:14:23.295
How is it?

00:14:23.295 --> 00:14:23.963
Good.

00:14:23.963 --> 00:14:26.265
Yeah.

00:14:34.206 --> 00:14:36.775
I like that we have these flowers

00:14:36.775 --> 00:14:39.778
You think you’re gonna be warm sleeping in your hammock?

00:14:40.279 --> 00:14:43.282
I'll try. There’s a bit of a draft.

00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:45.084
Yea, well

00:14:45.084 --> 00:14:47.620
 if it's too cold,

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:50.623
I can sleep in the car.

00:14:51.991 --> 00:14:54.260
In the seat, or?

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.263
No. It's a pretty long car

00:14:57.329 --> 00:15:00.332
It's, two meters from,

00:15:00.766 --> 00:15:01.967
behind the driver.

00:15:01.967 --> 00:15:04.970
So, I have a mattress

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:16.048
Because the blade runs like that.

00:15:16.048 --> 00:15:18.684
and if you touch it, like, here

00:15:18.684 --> 00:15:20.352
with full throttle...

00:15:20.352 --> 00:15:22.655
It will do that.

00:15:22.655 --> 00:15:24.490
because the chain goes like that.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:25.758
Especially if you have...

00:15:25.758 --> 00:15:29.995
So that's why you always cut like that

00:15:29.995 --> 00:15:31.897
or like that, underneath.

00:15:31.897 --> 00:15:35.301
But then the saw wants to go out,
so you have to push a little bit.

00:15:35.401 --> 00:15:38.304
You'll feel where the saw wants to go

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:41.473
and you do like half throttle

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.410
But this is the danger zone.

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:48.147
You can do it because see chainsaw
guys often like small branches

00:15:48.847 --> 00:15:50.282
The artists, you know.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:52.318
So you can do that.

00:15:52.318 --> 00:15:54.520
But usually

00:15:57.389 --> 00:15:58.524
like that.

00:15:58.524 --> 00:15:58.791
Yeah.

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:01.060
And then this
and it wants to bite in there

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.862
And that’s why the dog teeth are there

00:16:03.862 --> 00:16:06.665
So they pull the saw in

00:16:06.665 --> 00:16:07.967
And you move it a little git

00:16:07.967 --> 00:16:10.202
But you can also do like this.

00:16:10.202 --> 00:16:13.172
But then the saw wants to come out.

00:16:14.473 --> 00:16:17.343
So here this is, sort of, where you have to be careful

00:16:17.343 --> 00:16:19.345
Okay.

00:16:19.778 --> 00:16:21.714
And your stance needs to be

00:16:21.714 --> 00:16:24.450
especially on the hill...

00:16:34.526 --> 00:16:36.295
Yeah, I just got this one new

00:16:36.295 --> 00:16:38.931
it’s very strong

00:18:39.451 --> 00:18:41.520
Couscous!

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.922
By Ela.

00:19:18.957 --> 00:19:22.761
Does birch burn well?

00:19:23.996 --> 00:19:25.531
Yea! It gives a very white fire.

00:19:25.531 --> 00:19:27.099
It's a good one ?

00:19:27.099 --> 00:19:29.935
Yea it’s fine, but beech is the best

00:19:29.935 --> 00:19:31.503
a hard wood, it burns longer

00:19:42.447 --> 00:19:43.782
Go!

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:47.452
The big, wild world.

00:19:47.452 --> 00:19:49.988
You are free now.

00:19:54.593 --> 00:19:57.596
Yea I mean, we need to give them some space

00:19:57.596 --> 00:20:00.699
I give them first the food

00:20:00.699 --> 00:20:02.334
but give the food outside.

00:20:02.334 --> 00:20:04.503
Oh, yeah. You're right.

00:26:22.013 --> 00:26:29.888
the brown thing in the puree is ‘noce moscata’

00:26:29.888 --> 00:26:32.490
which is in english?

00:26:32.490 --> 00:26:35.093
nutmeg

00:26:35.093 --> 00:26:37.462
similar as in german

00:26:40.332 --> 00:26:42.534
in Dutch as well??

00:26:42.534 --> 00:26:45.003
Nootmuskaat

00:32:01.953 --> 00:32:03.288
Are you okay with your back?

00:32:03.288 --> 00:32:04.889
Do you want any help? 

00:32:04.889 --> 00:32:06.724
Yea I’m OK. I can use this in the wall.

00:34:58.596 --> 00:34:59.931
I wanted to show a walk through the...

00:34:59.931 --> 00:35:03.034
the open up pasture,
but there's not so much to see

00:35:04.202 --> 00:35:06.904
The weather is turning.

00:35:06.904 --> 00:35:09.907
And I'm very allergic to the pollen,

00:35:10.441 --> 00:35:13.411
which is the season now, but,

00:35:14.278 --> 00:35:16.147
Yeah, we cut a lot of birch here.

00:35:16.147 --> 00:35:19.150
We opened it up.

00:35:19.350 --> 00:35:21.486
Left, the healthiest trees standing

00:35:21.486 --> 00:35:24.922
so they can become wider and kind of thrive.

00:35:25.890 --> 00:35:28.893
But mostly this is farmland, so

00:35:29.060 --> 00:35:33.364
give space for the cows to graze
when they come in summer

00:35:34.098 --> 00:35:35.133
It's talking to Johannes

00:35:35.133 --> 00:35:40.471
He came here 11 years ago now, I think.

00:35:40.538 --> 00:35:43.007
And he also considered this place.

00:35:43.007 --> 00:35:45.710
But in the end,
he found that too much work

00:35:45.710 --> 00:35:48.112
He said that this was all free of trees

00:35:48.112 --> 00:35:51.115
all open pastures for

00:35:51.449 --> 00:35:52.884
cows and goats.

00:35:52.884 --> 00:35:54.552
But, you know,
through the years, it's just...

00:35:56.587 --> 00:35:59.590
All growing thick with birch, and some beech.

00:36:00.391 --> 00:36:02.560
So, Yeah.

00:36:02.560 --> 00:36:06.030
Yea we opened it up. A nice batch of firewood
for next years.

00:36:09.133 --> 00:36:10.835
Good place for grasses to grow.

00:36:10.835 --> 00:36:13.838
And wildflowers.

00:36:15.506 --> 00:36:17.008
Nice for a walk.

00:36:17.008 --> 00:36:18.142
Have some open space.

00:36:18.142 --> 00:36:21.512
So, yeah,
it's really exciting to see, but.

00:36:22.180 --> 00:36:23.114
Well, now it's foggy.

00:36:23.114 --> 00:36:24.849
There’s a lot of rain coming tomorrow.

00:36:24.849 --> 00:36:27.852
And the day after,

00:36:28.953 --> 00:36:29.453
I think during

00:36:29.453 --> 00:36:32.456
the landscape is really going to transform

00:36:32.790 --> 00:36:35.059
because, yeah, things are  blooming.

00:36:35.059 --> 00:36:38.062
First, the beech trees

00:36:38.462 --> 00:36:40.831
the big forest over there

00:36:40.831 --> 00:36:43.801
leaves are coming through very fast.

00:36:44.402 --> 00:36:47.772
Now the birch trees are starting
and the other ones as well.

00:36:47.772 --> 00:36:51.509
So I think after this weekend it's
gonna green up quite a lot

00:36:51.676 --> 00:36:54.612
with all the rain coming.

00:36:54.612 --> 00:36:56.948
We had sunny weather
for about three weeks.

00:36:56.948 --> 00:36:59.050
It's really beautiful
weather to work outside.

00:37:00.451 --> 00:37:03.087
Great help from the guys,

00:37:03.087 --> 00:37:06.090
help cutting down and collecting and,

00:37:06.390 --> 00:37:09.393
all the branches,

00:37:10.094 --> 00:37:13.231
the wood chipper wasn't available
for rent, so I have to do that again

00:37:13.231 --> 00:37:16.234
because there's a lot of branches
we need to,

00:37:16.801 --> 00:37:18.603
to mulch.

00:37:18.603 --> 00:37:21.272
But, yeah.

00:37:21.272 --> 00:37:23.741
Good progress.

00:37:23.741 --> 00:37:26.744
That's a cherry tree, the one over there.

00:37:26.978 --> 00:37:30.681
My dad discovered it
last year, or two years ago.

00:37:32.183 --> 00:37:33.251
It doesn't give fruit.

00:37:33.251 --> 00:37:34.552
It's just the only one here.

00:37:34.552 --> 00:37:37.622
But now it has a bit more light to grow.

00:37:38.389 --> 00:37:41.392
Same as that plum tree over there,
which you saw in the beginning.

00:37:41.492 --> 00:37:44.462
The white blossom.

00:37:44.595 --> 00:37:46.264
It's already disappearing now.

00:37:46.264 --> 00:37:48.733
Also doesn't give fruit,

00:37:48.733 --> 00:37:50.401
but the blossom is very beautiful.

00:37:50.401 --> 00:37:53.471
So now with a little bit more space,
it can can

00:37:53.571 --> 00:37:56.574
grow better.

00:37:57.174 --> 00:37:57.942
Yeah.

00:37:57.942 --> 00:37:59.610
Finishing the walls also.

00:37:59.610 --> 00:38:02.680
So that's going to be finished next week
I think another day or two.

00:38:03.481 --> 00:38:04.849
And pointing the walls

00:38:06.450 --> 00:38:08.486
work on the floor.

00:38:08.486 --> 00:38:10.755
And then I can, bring in a bandsaw.

00:38:10.755 --> 00:38:15.293
I saw a beautiful bandsaw
on Marketplace, from the 70s.

00:38:15.293 --> 00:38:18.062
I think he sent me some videos.

00:38:18.062 --> 00:38:20.398
It was working well,
but I have to go and see it

00:38:20.398 --> 00:38:23.100
It's far away, it’s from Modena,

00:38:23.100 --> 00:38:28.039
so, But I need to have the workshop floor
finished in order to bring in tools.

00:38:28.372 --> 00:38:30.841
So first finish that I want to have a bandsaw.

00:38:30.841 --> 00:38:36.180
I can work on the rain gutters,
which is going to have a lot of curved wood pieces

00:38:37.515 --> 00:38:40.184
the brackets to hold them up.

00:38:40.184 --> 00:38:41.619
So that's next.

00:38:41.619 --> 00:38:47.325
And work outside goes on as well, depending on the weather

